---
/**
 * Microsoft Clarity — heatmaps and session replay, project y8ayw5wcxw.
 *
 * Two things here are load-bearing and should not be tidied back toward the
 * snippet Microsoft hands you.
 *
 * 1. **It is a bundled script, not an inline one.** `script-src` is 'self'
 *    with no 'unsafe-inline' (public/_headers), and astro.config.mjs sets
 *    `assetsInlineLimit: 0` precisely so bundled scripts are emitted as files
 *    under /_astro and covered by 'self'. Pasted in inline, Clarity would be
 *    refused by the browser and would collect nothing at all — which is
 *    exactly how the Cloudflare beacon failed for weeks before it was removed
 *    (docs/launch/pre-launch-audit.md). The tag this script *fetches* is
 *    Microsoft's, so public/_headers still has to name *.clarity.ms as a
 *    script and connect origin.
 *
 * 2. **It runs on the real site only.** `import.meta.env.PROD` keeps it out of
 *    `astro dev`. The origin check keeps it out of the two other places a
 *    production build gets served — the GitHub Pages mirror and Cloudflare's
 *    *.pages.dev preview deployments — both of which build with the same
 *    environment and would otherwise mix sessions on URLs nobody is selling
 *    into the heatmaps for the ones we are.
 *
 * What this costs a visitor is written down on /privacy, in the section that
 * used to say the site ran no analytics. Change one and change the other.
 */
---

<script>
  import { CANONICAL_HOST } from '@/config/canonical-host';

  if (import.meta.env.PROD && window.location.origin === CANONICAL_HOST) {
    /* Microsoft's snippet, unminified. The queue has to exist before the tag
       lands so a clarity() call made in between is replayed rather than
       dropped; `arguments` is kept over rest args because it is Clarity's own
       code that reads these entries back. */
    const w = window as any;
    w.clarity =
      w.clarity ||
      function () {
        (w.clarity.q = w.clarity.q || []).push(arguments);
      };

    const tag = document.createElement('script');
    tag.async = true;
    tag.src = 'https://www.clarity.ms/tag/y8ayw5wcxw';
    document.head.appendChild(tag);
  }
</script>
